OL,3,GNEWSAVeteran conned by AI ex-soldier's
OL,4,A'pity scam'
OL,5,
OL,6,FExperts have warned of a growing wave
OL,7,Fof AI-generated "pity scams" using fake
OL,8,Fvideos of injured ex-military personnel
OL,9,Fto sell products online.
OL,11,FArmy veteran Raymond Gilbert, 63, from
OL,12,FBradenstoke, Wiltshire, said he was
OL,13,Fscammed by a TikTok account claiming to
OL,14,Fbelong to a fellow ex-serviceman.
OL,16,FHe spent #154.99 buying a "handmade"
OL,17,Fwooden flag that he said turned out to
OL,18,Fbe made in China. The BBC identified 45
OL,19,Fsimilar TikTok accounts, along with
OL,20,Fmore on other platforms, selling
OL,21,Fmilitary-themed items.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,342,340,200,160,0,100
